{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29561 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which (1S)-N-Methyl-Coclaurine may interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C, through a series of target-mediated pathways. The drug is implicated in the signaling cascade via Thymic stromal lymphopoietin, which is a known target of myrciacitrin III and 3alpha-Hydroxyolean-11-en-28,13beta-olide. These compounds are both capable of targeting Phosphodiesterase 6C, indicating a possible pathway where (1S)-N-Methyl-Coclaurine may act as a modulator of the signaling cascade through these intermediates. The high scores in all three paths suggest a strong, consistent relationship, with the drug potentially influencing the activity of Phosphodiesterase 6C through the activation or inhibition of downstream signaling molecules. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
